---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "First-pass Metabolism"
letter: "F"
anchor: "first-pass-metabolism"
category: "edibles"
---

The process by which orally consumed substances are metabolized by the liver before entering systemic circulation. When you eat a cannabis edible, THC travels through the digestive tract to the liver, where it's converted to 11-hydroxy-THC — a metabolite that crosses the blood-brain barrier more efficiently than THC itself. This is why edibles produce a more intense, longer-lasting, and more body-heavy effect than inhaled cannabis, even at the same dose.

→ [Cannabis Edibles 101](/edibles/cooking-with-cannabis-edibles-101/), [What Is THC?](/cannabis-101/what-is-thc/)
